WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:10.320
A newborn child bears no sin.

3
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:12.150
Garp.

4
00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:15.690
Take care of my child.

5
00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:20.800
Your father is...

6
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.470
the Pirate King, Gold Roger!

7
00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:43.290
Fire Fist Ace... is Gold Roger's son?!

8
00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:51.060
This is huge news!

9
00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:53.920
Call the main office right away! We're releasing an extra for this!

10
00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:57.870
So, it still lives...

11
00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:02.520
The...

12
00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:12.980
The blood of the Pirate King lives on!

13
00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:56.300
<b>Ace and Whitebeard</b>

14
00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:07.860
So, he isn't Luffy's real brother?

15
00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:16.200
Roger's...

16
00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.200
son?

17
00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:27.910
So his biological son lives on? What a miracle.

18
00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:32.640
Anyone who had a connection to Roger back then should have already been executed!

19
00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:38.390
Since he's Luffy-san's brother, I assumed Dragon was his father, too...

20
00:04:38.390 --> 00:04:41.490
I thought so too! What's going on here?

21
00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:44.130
Does this mean they aren't really brothers?

22
00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:50.370
Can you believe this, Garp?

23
00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:52.930
A child's about to be born...

24
00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:54.070
...My child.

25
00:04:56.980 --> 00:05:01.160
Unfortunately, I'll have left this world by the time that happens.

26
00:05:03.890 --> 00:05:07.090
And why are you telling this to me, a marine?

27
00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:08.500
Roger!

28
00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:13.960
The mother of that child, and any woman with ties to you, will undoubtedly be executed!

29
00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:19.230
That's why I'm telling you.

30
00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:28.310
The Government is sure to figure out where I've been this past year.

31
00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:31.420
They'll find her, and then they'll kill her.

32
00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:35.550
But... a newborn child bears no sin.

33
00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:42.520
Garp! You and I have nearly killed each other countless times.

34
00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:48.200
I trust you as much as I would a member of my own crew!

35
00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:00.870
Protect him for me.

36
00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:04.940
Don't try that selfish crap on me!

37
00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:08.650
No, I know you'll do it!

38
00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:20.500
Take care of my child!

39
00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:49.090
And you're sure this is the island?

40
00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:54.680
Roger was spotted here, but he was behaving differently.

41
00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:57.100
He was acting almost like a father.

42
00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:59.590
Roger's era is over.

43
00:06:59.590 --> 00:07:02.040
We must eradicate all traces of his bloodline.

44
00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:08.440
Investigate every child born during the ten months following his imprisonment.

45
00:07:15.210 --> 00:07:17.500
Investigate all pregnant women, as well.

46
00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:23.460
Kill any mother who seems suspicious.

47
00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:15.600
Five children were born this month.

48
00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:27.200
The following are expected to give birth next month...

49
00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:38.030
Not yet.

50
00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:44.310
You can't be born yet.

51
00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:50.920
I'm sorry.

52
00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:54.340
Not yet.

53
00:08:57.850 --> 00:08:59.420
Not yet.

54
00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:05.860
Not yet... Not yet...

55
00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:25.640
If you're a girl, your name will be Ann.

56
00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:30.930
If you're a boy, it'll be Ace.

57
00:09:31.980 --> 00:09:34.720
Those are the names he chose.

58
00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:40.460
Our child's name is Gol D. Ace.

59
00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:53.870
This is our child.

60
00:09:59.060 --> 00:09:59.960
Rouge!

61
00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:02.280
Rouge! Hang in there!

62
00:10:10.450 --> 00:10:12.690
You take care of him, Dadan!

63
00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:15.630
No way...!

64
00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:19.370
Whose kid is that?

65
00:10:23.370 --> 00:10:24.520
Dadan?

66
00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:27.900
That's right. From now on, this is where you'll be living.

67
00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:29.970
Huh?

68
00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:33.610
You're going to be living with these guys. Try to get along with them.

69
00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:41.320
As annoying as it is,

70
00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:46.000
both me and Luffy carry the blood of a world-renowned criminal.

71
00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:49.490
Even though I owe my mother a debt of gratitude and took the name "Portgas"...

72
00:10:49.490 --> 00:10:53.460
I still can't stand the thought that I carry the blood of that worthless father of mine.

73
00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:56.700
Gramps...

74
00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:59.370
My old man is...

75
00:11:02.270 --> 00:11:04.800
Whitebeard. And no one else.

76
00:11:08.550 --> 00:11:09.910
Garp...

77
00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:12.780
It's been two years now, hasn't it?

78
00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:17.830
Since you took the name of your mother, formed the Spade Pirates,

79
00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:23.260
and ventured to the seas with formidable strength and speed.

80
00:11:23.260 --> 00:11:26.430
At that point, we finally realized...

81
00:11:26.430 --> 00:11:30.400
...that we had not stopped Roger's bloodline!

82
00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:42.020
But Whitebeard, who realized this truth at the same time as us,

83
00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:45.640
decided to raise you to become the next Pirate King,

84
00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:49.700
and let the son of his former rival on to his own ship!

85
00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:53.120
That's not true!

86
00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:56.520
I got on that ship so I could make the old man the Pirate King!

87
00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:58.940
You're the only one who thinks that!

88
00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:03.310
We were careful not to act recklessly...

89
00:12:03.310 --> 00:12:06.400
You were under Whitebeard's protection!

90
00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:13.510
But left unchecked, you'd undoubtedly inspire a new generation of pirates.

91
00:12:13.510 --> 00:12:18.770
That is why your execution here today carries such great significance.

92
00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:26.260
Even if we must go to war against Whitebeard!

93
00:12:34.970 --> 00:12:36.470
Fleet Admiral Sengoku!

94
00:12:36.470 --> 00:12:38.000
Reporting in!

95
00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:41.310
The Gates of Justice are opening, but nobody's ordered them to!

96
00:12:41.310 --> 00:12:44.270
We can't get in touch with the control room, either!

97
00:12:44.270 --> 00:12:45.440
What?!

98
00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:00.800
They opened!

99
00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:02.560
What's going on here?!

100
00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:06.360
The Gates of Justice are opening on their own!

101
00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:10.140
Didn't the Navy say they wouldn't open it for us?

102
00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:17.800
The control room is most likely inside Marineford. Who could have done this?

103
00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:24.140
Here it comes! It is time!

104
00:13:24.140 --> 00:13:27.500
C-Captain Buggy, it can't be...!

105
00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:29.950
The time has come!

106
00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:31.800
Don't tell me, you're...!

107
00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:34.560
I never realized you were actually God's messenger!

108
00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:36.270
Seriously?! Buggy!

109
00:13:36.270 --> 00:13:39.660
Of course it's not true! There must be some sort of trick here!

110
00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:44.140
He's right... Who the hell opened the Gate?!

111
00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:49.070
No...! Could Heaven itself want to make me the Pirate King?!

112
00:13:54.590 --> 00:13:56.420
They're here!

113
00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:58.720
All troops, prepare for battle!

114
00:14:06.690 --> 00:14:10.500
They appeared so suddenly! But where did they come from?!

115
00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:23.480
It's a huge fleet of pirate ships!

116
00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:26.150
Where is Whitebeard? Find him!

117
00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:29.180
"Bohemian Knight" Doma!

118
00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:30.450
"Thunder Lord" McGuy!

119
00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:32.780
The DeCalvan Brothers!

120
00:14:33.420 --> 00:14:35.020
"Whirl Spider" Squard!

121
00:14:35.590 --> 00:14:41.010
Every one of these mighty figures... They're all captains renowned throughout the New World!

122
00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:43.600
There are forty-three ships in total.

123
00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:46.470
Whitebeard and his commanders are nowhere to be found.

124
00:14:46.470 --> 00:14:50.370
But these pirates are definitely allied with Whitebeard!

125
00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:52.420
Can you see Ace-chan?

126
00:14:52.420 --> 00:14:54.780
There he is! Ace!

127
00:14:58.360 --> 00:15:01.400
Don't get thrown off by this! You're all hopeless!

128
00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:05.320
You guys...?

129
00:15:05.320 --> 00:15:06.850
Shall we attack them?

130
00:15:06.850 --> 00:15:10.450
No, wait. Whitebeard's must be around here somewhere!

131
00:15:10.450 --> 00:15:14.200
He's waiting for the right moment. Watch the water!

132
00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:19.030
Now it's getting interesting! I'm really getting excited here!

133
00:15:19.030 --> 00:15:21.100
Hurry and show up, Whitebeard!

134
00:15:39.590 --> 00:15:40.920
It can't be!

135
00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:48.390
Where is he coming from?

136
00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:53.730
Well, he sure picked one amazing place to show up.

137
00:15:53.730 --> 00:15:56.300
We never considered this!

138
00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:08.490
There's a shadow beneath the surface!

139
00:16:08.490 --> 00:16:09.650
No way!

140
00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:21.140
So that's how they did it?

141
00:16:21.140 --> 00:16:26.580
They coated their entire fleet and came here along the bottom of the sea!

142
00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:45.250
It's the Moby Dick!

143
00:17:01.070 --> 00:17:04.600
Three more of Whitebeard's ships have appeared!

144
00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:11.460
They've broken into the bay!

145
00:17:13.740 --> 00:17:15.410
T-That's...

146
00:17:15.410 --> 00:17:17.950
The commander of the First Division, Marco!

147
00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:23.760
All 14 commanders are here!

148
00:17:51.080 --> 00:17:54.220
How long has it been, Sengoku?

149
00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:56.750
Whitebeard!

150
00:17:56.750 --> 00:17:59.160
I take it my beloved son...

151
00:18:00.030 --> 00:18:02.330
is still doing well?

152
00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:16.780
How could you get in here so easily...?!

153
00:18:23.480 --> 00:18:24.870
Vwe've made it past the gates!

154
00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:31.330
Now then, Vi wonder if vyou and Ace-boy's father will show up.

155
00:18:31.330 --> 00:18:32.460
Ace's father?

156
00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:37.260
Since his son Ace is about to be executed, Vi'm sure Dragon will do something!

157
00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:40.260
Oh, me and Ace don't have the same dad.

158
00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:44.450
My dad is Dragon...

159
00:18:44.450 --> 00:18:47.470
but Ace's dad is Gold Roger.

160
00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:48.340
What?!

161
00:18:49.240 --> 00:18:52.300
I never got to meet him, but I hear he's pretty amazing.

162
00:18:52.300 --> 00:18:55.110
But Ace gets mad whenever I say that.

163
00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:56.390
What?!

164
00:18:56.390 --> 00:18:58.470
Oh, yeah. That's supposed to be a secret.

165
00:18:58.470 --> 00:19:01.490
What?!

166
00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:16.330
Wait just a little longer, Ace.

167
00:19:22.310 --> 00:19:24.400
Old man!

168
00:19:43.590 --> 00:19:45.270
W-What?

169
00:19:45.270 --> 00:19:46.630
A crack... in the air?!

170
00:19:57.860 --> 00:19:59.970
What kind of blast is that?!

171
00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:02.610
Not good! Look at the size of that wave!

172
00:20:02.610 --> 00:20:06.520
A seaquake?! He can make even the oceans shake?!

173
00:20:06.520 --> 00:20:08.720
There's one on the other side, too!

174
00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:10.750
Is this Whitebeard's power?!

175
00:20:14.090 --> 00:20:16.190
I'm going on ahead!

176
00:20:21.270 --> 00:20:23.270
Take care, Ace!

177
00:20:23.270 --> 00:20:25.970
Sure! So long, Luffy!

178
00:20:25.970 --> 00:20:31.710
Yeah! When I set out to sea in three years, I'll have gotten even stronger!

179
00:20:31.710 --> 00:20:32.820
Yeah!

180
00:20:34.350 --> 00:20:36.850
Ace!

181
00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:47.760
Now, let's go cause some trouble!

182
00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:52.860
That kid...! He went and became a pirate?!

183
00:20:52.860 --> 00:20:56.130
A pirate ship! It's a flag I've never seen before!

184
00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:06.640
This is a pirate who's been growing in strength recently.

185
00:21:06.640 --> 00:21:09.100
D...? Where is he from?

186
00:21:09.100 --> 00:21:14.490
We don't know yet, but he's a rookie who wields the power of a Logia Devil Fruit!

187
00:21:16.510 --> 00:21:20.470
A kid with some strength has shown up in the Grand Line!

188
00:21:20.470 --> 00:21:23.290
It seems he turned down an offer to join the Seven Warlords.

189
00:21:23.290 --> 00:21:28.220
How old are these kids?

190
00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:30.940
Why do the young ones always have to be in such a hurry?

191
00:21:31.800 --> 00:21:34.340
Are you serious, Captain?!

192
00:21:34.340 --> 00:21:36.010
I want to meet him, no matter what!

193
00:21:36.340 --> 00:21:38.180
Red-Haired Shanks!

194
00:21:39.240 --> 00:21:41.580
The Spade Pirates?

195
00:21:42.080 --> 00:21:47.190
The famous Super Rookies... have come for me?

196
00:21:47.190 --> 00:21:49.840
No, that's not what I'm here for!

197
00:21:49.840 --> 00:21:53.690
You saved my little brother's life. He always talks about you.

198
00:21:53.690 --> 00:21:56.130
I just wanted to thank you in person.

199
00:21:56.130 --> 00:21:57.290
You mean Luffy?!

200
00:21:58.270 --> 00:22:00.060
I never knew he had a brother!

201
00:22:00.060 --> 00:22:03.070
I see. I'm glad you came!

202
00:22:03.070 --> 00:22:05.200
Please, tell me more!

203
00:22:05.700 --> 00:22:07.600
Let's have a party!

204
00:22:12.080 --> 00:22:15.480
Hey, big guy! I wanna meet this Whitebeard!

205
00:22:15.480 --> 00:22:20.610
I'm not going to allow a kid with murderous intent to see the old man!

206
00:22:20.610 --> 00:22:22.750
Captain! That's Jinbe!

207
00:22:22.750 --> 00:22:25.610
Really? One of the Seven Warlords?

208
00:22:25.610 --> 00:22:28.280
Well, that's gonna be a problem.

209
00:22:28.280 --> 00:22:32.170
I may not be a member of the Whitebeard Pirates...

210
00:22:32.170 --> 00:22:35.270
but I feel it is my duty to face you!

211
00:22:44.990 --> 00:22:49.250
It's been five days, and they're still fighting!

212
00:22:49.250 --> 00:22:51.650
They might both die at this rate!

213
00:23:03.290 --> 00:23:06.010
Ace!

214
00:23:13.740 --> 00:23:15.640
What's that?!

215
00:23:16.140 --> 00:23:20.510
Where's the kid who wants to take my head?

216
00:23:23.110 --> 00:23:27.420
As you wish, I'll take you on!

217
00:23:28.520 --> 00:23:30.820
It's the Whitebeard Pirates!

218
00:23:31.690 --> 00:23:34.790
I'll take care of this myself.

219
00:23:43.340 --> 00:23:44.800
You guys!

220
00:23:49.680 --> 00:23:52.660
Captain! Captain Ace, what are you doing?!

221
00:23:52.660 --> 00:23:54.210
Run, you guys!

222
00:23:54.210 --> 00:23:56.080
Captain!

223
00:23:57.850 --> 00:24:01.520
What? You're gonna run away now?

224
00:24:01.520 --> 00:24:03.570
I'm letting my crew escape.

225
00:24:03.570 --> 00:24:06.590
I'm staying in their place. I won't run!

226
00:24:07.490 --> 00:24:10.930
What a cheeky little brat you are!

227
00:24:22.380 --> 00:24:23.780
I'm...

228
00:24:26.280 --> 00:24:28.050
You still tryin' to stand up?

229
00:24:30.480 --> 00:24:34.610
I'd hate to see you die here, kid.

230
00:24:34.610 --> 00:24:36.430
If you still want to fight,

231
00:24:36.430 --> 00:24:41.260
then take my name and roam the seas wild and free!

232
00:24:45.900 --> 00:24:47.870
Become my son!

233
00:24:48.700 --> 00:24:50.920
You've gotta be kidding me!

234
00:24:56.750 --> 00:25:00.000
I'm the commander of the Fourth Division... Thatch!

235
00:25:00.500 --> 00:25:02.400
Since you're joining our crew,

236
00:25:03.870 --> 00:25:05.150
I think we should be friends.

237
00:25:05.150 --> 00:25:06.770
Shut up!

238
00:25:08.900 --> 00:25:10.990
You sure woke up in a bad mood.

239
00:25:10.990 --> 00:25:14.890
Oh, yeah. Do you want to know what happened after you passed out?

240
00:25:15.470 --> 00:25:21.870
Your companions came to get you back... so we beat them all.

241
00:25:21.870 --> 00:25:26.300
What? It's not like they're dead.
We're keeping them here on this ship.

242
00:25:26.890 --> 00:25:30.500
Are you sure you should leave me like this, without any locks or shackles or anything?

243
00:25:30.500 --> 00:25:33.710
Shackles? We don't need those!

244
00:25:55.790 --> 00:25:58.450
Hey, hey, what d'ya think your doing?

245
00:25:58.450 --> 00:26:01.200
You should be more considerate at this time of night!

246
00:26:15.410 --> 00:26:17.400
Hey, he fell overboard!

247
00:26:17.400 --> 00:26:18.600
And he can't swim, either!

248
00:26:18.600 --> 00:26:20.260
Someone, go save him!

249
00:26:22.730 --> 00:26:27.680
He does this every day. He has real persistence.

250
00:26:28.890 --> 00:26:30.220
Was that the hundredth time?

251
00:26:30.220 --> 00:26:31.500
I think so.

252
00:26:48.390 --> 00:26:49.650
You guys...

253
00:26:50.840 --> 00:26:53.860
Why do you call him your father, anyway?

254
00:26:56.130 --> 00:27:00.590
Because he calls us his sons.

255
00:27:01.430 --> 00:27:04.970
To the rest of the world we're all just outcasts.

256
00:27:05.860 --> 00:27:07.860
It makes us happy.

257
00:27:07.860 --> 00:27:12.210
It's just a word, but it makes us happy!

258
00:27:20.410 --> 00:27:24.720
Hey, how long are you gonna keep risking your life like this?

259
00:27:25.670 --> 00:27:27.530
Make up your mind already!

260
00:27:28.130 --> 00:27:31.400
You won't be able to take pops' head in your current condition.

261
00:27:32.450 --> 00:27:35.560
Are you gonna get off this ship and start over...

262
00:27:36.820 --> 00:27:38.560
or are you gonna stay here...

263
00:27:40.860 --> 00:27:43.660
and take on Whitebeard's mark?

264
00:27:50.980 --> 00:27:52.840
You're Doma, right?

265
00:27:56.940 --> 00:28:00.230
Wow! Ace did it again!

266
00:28:00.230 --> 00:28:03.260
He made Doma's crew surrender, all on his own!

267
00:28:03.260 --> 00:28:05.730
Me, become the Second Division Commander?

268
00:28:05.730 --> 00:28:08.800
We've haven't had one for a long time.

269
00:28:08.800 --> 00:28:10.700
Everybody would definitely accept you!

270
00:28:12.970 --> 00:28:17.530
You've been here a lot longer than I have, right? Are you sure it's okay?

271
00:28:18.640 --> 00:28:20.830
It's fine, don't worry about it.

272
00:28:20.830 --> 00:28:23.850
I don't have that kind of ambition anyway.

273
00:28:25.120 --> 00:28:28.190
Go ahead, Commander Ace!

274
00:28:32.920 --> 00:28:35.350
Really? What a surprise!

275
00:28:35.350 --> 00:28:36.930
So, that's how it is?

276
00:28:39.420 --> 00:28:42.670
You don't really act like Roger, though...

277
00:28:43.660 --> 00:28:45.760
Wasn't he your enemy?

278
00:28:45.760 --> 00:28:47.430
Aren't you gonna throw me out?

279
00:28:47.430 --> 00:28:53.860
When you said you had something 
important to talk about, I thought it would be more important than this...

280
00:28:53.860 --> 00:28:57.880
It doesn't matter who your parents were. Everyone is a child of the sea.

281
00:29:07.950 --> 00:29:11.190
It looks like another incredible man has joined Whitebeard's crew.

282
00:29:11.190 --> 00:29:13.500
They say he's unbelievably strong!

283
00:29:31.310 --> 00:29:34.220
Stop it, Ace! Calm down!

284
00:29:34.220 --> 00:29:37.170
The old man said he'd make an exception, just this once!

285
00:29:37.170 --> 00:29:38.890
You don't have to chase after Teach!

286
00:29:38.890 --> 00:29:41.990
Let me go! He was a member of my division!

287
00:29:41.990 --> 00:29:46.450
If I just ignore this, Thatch won't be able to rest in peace!

288
00:29:47.020 --> 00:29:48.170
Ace.

289
00:29:50.160 --> 00:29:53.800
It's fine, just this once.

290
00:29:53.800 --> 00:29:57.130
I have a weird feeling about this.

291
00:29:57.130 --> 00:30:00.340
He killed a crewmate and escaped!

292
00:30:00.530 --> 00:30:03.180
After living under your protection for so many years...

293
00:30:03.180 --> 00:30:05.550
he just spat right in your face!

294
00:30:07.650 --> 00:30:10.500
Above all else, he tarnished his father's name.

295
00:30:10.500 --> 00:30:12.790
Do you think I can just ignore that?

296
00:30:12.980 --> 00:30:15.530
I'll settle this!

297
00:30:20.930 --> 00:30:23.900
Hey, wait! Come back, Ace!

298
00:30:24.690 --> 00:30:26.000
Ace!

299
00:30:35.760 --> 00:30:37.470
Old man...

300
00:30:38.940 --> 00:30:40.140
All of you...

301
00:30:43.390 --> 00:30:48.760
I ignored your orders and ran off! Why didn't you just abandon me?!

302
00:30:48.760 --> 00:30:50.990
This only happened because I was so stubborn!

303
00:30:53.750 --> 00:30:54.730
No...

304
00:30:57.770 --> 00:31:01.570
I was the one who told you to go...

305
00:31:02.770 --> 00:31:04.360
my son.

306
00:31:08.660 --> 00:31:11.410
You're lying! Don't be ridiculous!

307
00:31:11.410 --> 00:31:13.990
You tried to stop me back then, but I...!

308
00:31:13.990 --> 00:31:16.750
I told you to go!

309
00:31:22.260 --> 00:31:27.430
I told him to go. Isn't that right, Marco?

310
00:31:27.600 --> 00:31:33.040
Yeah, I heard it too. We sent you into a lot of trouble, huh, Ace?

311
00:31:33.290 --> 00:31:36.670
This entire ocean should know...

312
00:31:37.840 --> 00:31:40.210
what happens when someone...

313
00:31:40.210 --> 00:31:44.560
harms one of our crewmates.

314
00:31:46.370 --> 00:31:51.410
Anyone who hurts you won't be allowed to live, Ace!

315
00:31:51.410 --> 00:31:53.390
Hang on! We're coming for you, right now!

316
00:31:59.660 --> 00:32:02.730
Prepare yourselves, Navy HQ!

317
00:32:09.010 --> 00:32:11.910
He's gathered quite an impressive group, huh?

318
00:32:11.910 --> 00:32:15.000
What are they going on about?

319
00:32:16.100 --> 00:32:18.250
I've got a bad feeling about this.

320
00:32:26.240 --> 00:32:28.560
What are these tremors?!

321
00:32:28.560 --> 00:32:33.260
Here it comes. The seaquake that he set off earlier...

322
00:32:33.260 --> 00:32:36.070
is coming back as a tsunami!

323
00:32:42.370 --> 00:32:44.940
The earthquake man, who ate the Tremor-Tremor Fruit...

324
00:32:44.940 --> 00:32:48.950
"Whitebeard", Edward Newgate!

325
00:32:52.150 --> 00:32:53.620
What is that?!

326
00:32:53.620 --> 00:32:55.620
It's a tsunami! It's huge!

327
00:32:55.620 --> 00:33:00.410
We might outnumber them, but don't assume that it guarantees our victory...

328
00:33:00.410 --> 00:33:04.550
It's possible that we will be the ones to meet our end!

329
00:33:04.550 --> 00:33:06.100
That man...

330
00:33:07.200 --> 00:33:10.370
has the power to destroy the world!

331
00:33:19.540 --> 00:33:21.310
It's starting...

332
00:33:21.310 --> 00:33:22.740
The war!

333
00:33:25.850 --> 00:33:27.720
Let's go!

334
00:33:37.290 --> 00:33:43.300
Whitebeard and his fleet of fourty-seven pirate ships from the New World are attacking.

335
00:33:43.300 --> 00:33:46.170
Standing against them are the
Government's two greatest forces:

336
00:33:46.170 --> 00:33:49.110
Navy HQ and the
Seven Royal Warlords of the Sea.

337
00:33:50.040 --> 00:33:53.350
No matter who the winner is... no matter who the loser is...

338
00:33:53.350 --> 00:33:54.880
the era will change.
